# transport.kb — how people and goods move, and the infrastructure that lets them.
#
# `technology.kb` has `vehicle`, `car`, `train`, `aircraft`, `ship` and `bicycle` — six lines that
# say what a thing is and nothing about the system it belongs to. The general knowledge here is
# mostly *system* knowledge: a road is not a vehicle, an airport is not an aeroplane, a licence is
# not a wheel, and none of those had a fact.
#
# `everyday.kb` has `road` and `traffic light`; this file is the layer above them.

# --- modes ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- #
transport | is_a=activity | means=moving people or goods from one place to another | has_kind=road transport | has_kind=rail transport | has_kind=water transport | has_kind=air transport | requires=a vehicle | requires=a route
road transport | is_a=transport | requires=roads | has_kind=car | has_kind=bus | has_kind=truck | has_property=door to door | has_property=flexible in route
rail transport | is_a=transport | requires=track | has_property=efficient for heavy loads over land | has_property=fixed route
water transport | is_a=transport | requires=a waterway | has_property=the cheapest way to move bulk goods far | has_property=slow
air transport | is_a=transport | has_property=the fastest way to travel far | has_property=the most expensive per tonne | requires=an airport
public transport | is_a=transport | means=shared transport open to anyone who pays a fare | has_kind=bus | has_kind=metro | has_kind=train | causes=less congestion than the same journeys by car
freight | is_a=transport | means=the carriage of goods rather than people | requires=loading and unloading
logistics | is_a=activity | means=planning how goods get from where they are made to where they are needed | involves=warehousing | involves=routing

# --- road vehicles -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- #
bus | is_a=vehicle | is_a=public transport | purpose=carrying many passengers along a fixed route | has_property=cheaper per passenger than a car
truck | is_a=vehicle | purpose=carrying goods by road | also_known_as=lorry | has_property=heavy
motorcycle | is_a=vehicle | has_property=two wheels and an engine | has_property=cheap to run | requires=a helmet for safety
scooter | is_a=vehicle | has_property=small wheels and a step through frame | purpose=short urban journeys
auto rickshaw | is_a=vehicle | has_property=three wheels | located_in=South Asia | purpose=short hired journeys
bullock cart | is_a=vehicle | requires=draught animals | purpose=carrying loads on rural tracks
ambulance | is_a=vehicle | purpose=carrying a patient to hospital quickly | has_property=right of way over other traffic | has_part=siren
fire engine | is_a=vehicle | purpose=carrying firefighters, water and ladders to a fire
tractor trailer | is_a=vehicle | purpose=hauling large loads | has_part=trailer
electric vehicle | is_a=vehicle | requires=a battery | requires=charging | causes=no exhaust emissions at the point of use | has_property=quieter than an engine
hybrid vehicle | is_a=vehicle | consists_of=an engine and an electric motor | purpose=lower fuel use in town

# --- how a vehicle works -------------------------------------------------------------------------- #
engine | is_a=machine | purpose=turning fuel into motion | has_kind=internal combustion engine | has_kind=jet engine | requires=fuel
transmission | is_a=machine part | purpose=passing the engine's power to the wheels at a useful speed | has_part=gear
gear | is_a=machine part | purpose=trading speed for turning force | has_property=toothed
clutch | is_a=machine part | purpose=connecting and disconnecting the engine from the transmission
brake | is_a=machine part | purpose=slowing or stopping a vehicle | causes=kinetic energy turning into heat | requires=friction
tyre | is_a=vehicle part | consists_of=rubber | purpose=gripping the road and cushioning the ride | requires=correct air pressure
steering wheel | is_a=vehicle part | purpose=pointing the front wheels
axle | is_a=machine part | purpose=carrying a pair of wheels and letting them turn
chassis | is_a=vehicle part | purpose=the frame everything else is mounted on
suspension | is_a=vehicle part | purpose=keeping the wheels on the road over bumps | causes=a smoother ride
speedometer | is_a=instrument | purpose=showing how fast a vehicle is going
fuel | is_a=substance | purpose=supplying the energy an engine burns | has_kind=petrol | has_kind=diesel | has_kind=compressed natural gas
petrol | is_a=fuel | purpose=fuelling spark ignition engines | occurs_when=crude oil is refined
diesel | is_a=fuel | purpose=fuelling compression ignition engines | has_property=more energy per litre than petrol

# --- rail ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- #
railway | is_a=infrastructure | has_part=track | has_part=station | has_part=signal | purpose=carrying trains
track | is_a=infrastructure | consists_of=rails | consists_of=sleepers | purpose=guiding and carrying a train | has_property=a fixed gauge
locomotive | is_a=vehicle | purpose=pulling a train | has_kind=steam locomotive | has_kind=diesel locomotive | has_kind=electric locomotive
carriage | is_a=vehicle | purpose=carrying passengers in a train | also_known_as=coach
railway station | is_a=building | purpose=where passengers join and leave a train | has_part=railway platform
railway platform | is_a=structure | purpose=letting passengers step level into a train
railway signal | is_a=device | purpose=telling a driver whether the line ahead is clear | causes=trains being kept apart
level crossing | is_a=structure | means=where a road crosses a railway on the same level | causes=danger if the barrier is ignored
metro | is_a=rail transport | is_a=public transport | located_in=cities | has_property=usually underground or elevated | purpose=moving many people across a city quickly
tram | is_a=vehicle | is_a=public transport | located_in=city streets | requires=rails laid in the road
high speed rail | is_a=rail transport | has_property=runs far faster than conventional trains | requires=dedicated track

# --- water --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- #
boat | is_a=vehicle | located_in=water | purpose=carrying people or goods on water | requires=buoyancy
ferry | is_a=boat | purpose=carrying passengers and vehicles across water on a fixed route
cargo ship | is_a=ship | purpose=carrying goods across oceans | has_property=the cheapest way to move bulk far
container ship | is_a=cargo ship | purpose=carrying standard steel containers | causes=much faster loading than loose cargo
tanker | is_a=ship | purpose=carrying oil or other liquids in bulk
submarine | is_a=vehicle | capable_of=travelling under water | requires=ballast tanks to sink and rise
sail | is_a=vehicle part | purpose=catching wind to drive a boat | requires=wind
anchor | is_a=equipment | purpose=holding a vessel in one place | requires=weight and a grip on the bottom
rudder | is_a=vehicle part | purpose=steering a boat or aircraft
port | is_a=infrastructure | purpose=where ships load and unload | has_part=dock | has_part=crane | located_in=a coast or a river mouth
canal | is_a=waterway | means=an artificial channel cut for boats or for water | purpose=shortening a route or carrying irrigation water
lighthouse | is_a=building | purpose=warning ships away from a hazard | located_in=a headland or a rock | has_part=lamp
buoy | is_a=marker | purpose=marking a channel or a hazard in water | has_property=floats and is anchored

# --- air and space ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- #
aeroplane | is_a=vehicle | capable_of=flight | has_part=wing | has_part=jet engine | has_part=fuselage | requires=a runway | requires=lift
wing | is_a=vehicle part | purpose=generating lift | has_property=curved on top so air moves faster over it
lift force | is_a=force | means=the upward force that holds an aircraft up | requires=air moving over a wing | causes=flight
drag | is_a=force | means=the resistance of air to something moving through it | causes=fuel being burned to keep speed up
thrust | is_a=force | means=the forward force an engine produces | causes=an aircraft accelerating
jet engine | is_a=engine | purpose=producing thrust by pushing air backwards | requires=fuel and air
propeller | is_a=machine part | purpose=producing thrust by turning blades | located_in=aircraft and boats
helicopter | is_a=vehicle | capable_of=hovering | capable_of=taking off vertically | has_part=rotor | purpose=reaching places without a runway
rotor | is_a=vehicle part | purpose=producing lift and thrust by spinning | located_in=a helicopter
airport | is_a=infrastructure | purpose=where aircraft take off, land and are serviced | has_part=runway | has_part=terminal | has_part=control tower
runway | is_a=structure | purpose=the strip an aircraft accelerates along to take off
air traffic control | is_a=service | purpose=keeping aircraft safely apart | requires=radar | requires=radio
cockpit | is_a=part of a vehicle | purpose=where the pilot sits and controls the aircraft
pilot | is_a=person | purpose=flying an aircraft | requires=a licence | requires=training
black box | is_a=device | purpose=recording flight data and cockpit voices | has_property=built to survive a crash | also_known_as=flight recorder

# --- the network and its rules --------------------------------------------------------------------------------- #
road | purpose=carrying vehicles between places | has_kind=highway | has_kind=street | has_kind=expressway | consists_of=asphalt
highway | is_a=road | purpose=carrying traffic between towns at speed
expressway | is_a=road | has_property=no crossings at the same level | has_property=access only at interchanges
bridge | is_a=structure | purpose=carrying a route over an obstacle | has_kind=arch bridge | has_kind=suspension bridge | requires=support at each end
tunnel | is_a=structure | purpose=carrying a route through an obstacle | located_in=under ground or water
flyover | is_a=bridge | purpose=carrying one road over another | causes=less waiting at a junction
roundabout | is_a=junction | purpose=letting traffic from several roads merge without stopping
junction | is_a=structure | means=where two or more routes meet
zebra crossing | is_a=road marking | purpose=giving people on foot a place to cross | causes=vehicles being required to stop
traffic sign | is_a=sign | purpose=telling drivers what the rules are here | has_kind=stop sign | has_kind=speed limit sign
speed limit | is_a=rule | means=the fastest a vehicle may legally go here | purpose=reducing the severity of crashes
traffic jam | is_a=condition | occurs_when=more vehicles want to use a road than it can carry | causes=delay | causes=more fuel burnt
congestion | is_a=condition | means=traffic moving far below the road's design speed | causes=lost time and higher emissions
driving licence | is_a=document | purpose=permitting a person to drive | requires=a test
seat belt | is_a=safety device | purpose=holding an occupant in place in a crash | causes=far fewer serious injuries
helmet | is_a=safety device | purpose=protecting the head | requires=being fastened to work
airbag | is_a=safety device | purpose=cushioning an occupant in a crash | occurs_when=a severe impact is detected
toll | is_a=charge | purpose=paying for a road or bridge from those who use it
fare | is_a=charge | means=what a passenger pays for a journey on public transport
timetable | is_a=document | purpose=saying when a service departs and arrives
navigation | is_a=activity | means=working out where one is and how to get where one is going | requires=a map or a positioning system
